# RTL and Persian

- `dir="rtl"` and `lang="fa"` are set once on `<html>`. Never patch direction per component.
- Numbers, currency, technical IDs, codes (e.g. `Adm-Dsc-2N1`, discount codes), URLs, emails and Latin text inside
  Persian sentences are wrapped in a `dir="ltr"` span (use the shared `Ltr`/`Bdi` helper, or `<bdi>`).
- Layout uses logical properties only (see `10-design-system.mdc`).
- User-visible strings live in the message catalog, not in components. Keys are namespaced by service
  (`dsc.*`, `nws.*`, `common.*`); SRS-quoted texts use code-based keys (`40-srs-traceability.mdc`).
- Text normalization: store and display Persian `ی`/`ک` (not Arabic `ي`/`ك`); normalize user input in search and
  duplicate-name checks the same way, and normalize Persian/Arabic digits to Latin before sending to the API.
- Digits: display policy (Persian or Latin digits) is defined once in the formatting util and applied everywhere
  through it. Never format numbers inline.
- Dates: Jalali (Shamsi) for display via ONE shared date util and ONE date/date-range picker; send ISO-8601 to the
  API. Never use `toLocaleDateString` ad hoc. Relative times ("۵ دقیقه پیش") come from the same util.
- Money: always show the unit (تومان/ریال, per the formatting util). Amounts come from the server — never compute
  prices, discounts, wallet balances or fees client-side for submitted operations.
- Use ZWNJ (نیم‌فاصله) correctly in copy; do not replace it with spaces.
- Font: the project Persian font from the design system, loaded through the framework font loader with a fallback
  stack.
